A||X||69||Cliff Pennock||About the closed threads||||1||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||05-22-2001||06:34 AM||||Geez Louise, I leave the forum alone for a few hours to get some sleep and look what happens...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Seriously, I've closed the two Carisle threads and Lisa's "I'M GONE" thread because I simply can't understand why people are wasting my diskspace and bandwidth over such trivial things.<P>I thought we were a close community here - you know, the "proud owner of a Fiero and proud member of PFF" kinda stuff. Heck, some of you that are now flaming each other even met and exchanged a few friendly words only 3 days ago.<P>We've all worked hard to create this place. And we ended up with a friendly and helpful place where we could discuss all-things-Fiero (and much, much more) amongst some of the nicest and funniest people on the internet.<P>Of course, even in the closest of families there will be arguments but I fail to see why this has to be taken to a point where we start tearing down the house we live in, and scare away some of the most valued family members. Especially since the end result can only be that we are left with ruins of something that used to be a place we liked to call our home. Maybe I'm over-reacting a bit since in reality, this is of course nothing more than a collection of files on a computer somewhere - but still.<P>So I closed those threads.<P>I hope Lisa reads this and decides she will not leave. I hope <B>everybody</B> reads this and decide that flamewars have no place on this forum. I hope that people realize that you can have a difference of opinion without downright insulting the other party. Think about the alternative. That someday you'll type in "www.fiero.nl" and you'll get a pop-up message stating "Server not found".<P>Now shake hands and make up!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||05-22-2001||06:48 AM||||SLEEPIN'?? Cliff, you were sleepin'? What the HECK were you thinkin'?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks for closing those two threads before the embers could flare up again... I think things had pretty well burned out, but better safe than sorry...<P>It's nice to have a 'home' online, even when things get heated... that's life - not everyone is going to agree all the time...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for this place, Cliff. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||05-22-2001||07:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>I simply can't understand why people are wasting my diskspace and bandwidth over such trivial things.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's pushing is cliff... Wasting your bandwidth and diskspace?    Come on.....<P>Honestly, I went to bed HOURS before you closed them, I agree I probably stepped over the line, not that it wasn't somewhat warranted.  The conversation was somewhat fuelled by off-list issues which I should not have brought here, for that, I apoligize.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Predator||05-22-2001||07:42 AM||||Sheesh, I just read through all that. I usually just ignore threads like those as soon as I see it is turning bad. Your right Cliff those got way out of hand. I aggree here latley it has gotten where I have to think twice before replying to a thread so I can word everything politically correct so the flame war won't start. I came here originally to get information on working on my car, but latley most of the threads have been people just bashing each other. If anybody makes a comment that even hints of a disagreement on a subject then it all starts up. I hope all these attacks against other members stops soon. I hate to see someone get to the point where their feelings are hurt so bad that they quit coming here. Cliff you do a great service with this forum to our community, and I hope it never comes to the point where you feel you have to shut it down. Thanks for the space  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000004||Songman||05-22-2001||07:56 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Wasting your bandwidth and diskspace?    Come on.....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Shhhh... Yes, it is his bandwidth and diskspace. Cliff foots the bill for all of this out of his own pocket. Not to mention all of the work he puts in. He has the right to not want to see a very successful forum killed over trivialities. Everyone remember, if not for Cliff's willingness to do this, we could lose this forum that we all love so much.<P>I'm sure everyone has a dose of reality now, Cliff, and maybe we can all get back on track. Thanks again for all you do.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroHarry||05-22-2001||08:09 AM||||I think the vast majority here appreciate everything Cliff has done here on the Forum.<BR>This is the best thing going, on the web for all Fiero lover's to be involved in.<BR>Cliff, as to pics of members, well I only saw one person wearing a Forum tee-shirt, I think it was Bob Schlag (Bob if I mis-spelled that Im very sorry).<BR>Most of us didnt get our shirts ready in time for Carlisle.<BR>But I saw a whole bunch with signs in the cars.<P>Carlisle was a blast for me. I didnt realize just how many HMN there are out there that are in such good condition.<P>I think every one who attended had a great time, and all deserve recognition for all there hard work.<P>As soon as I get a my software back for this memory stick I got I'll find some way to make available all 377 pictures I got while I was there.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 263K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by FieroHarry (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||05-22-2001||08:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B> That's pushing is cliff... Wasting your bandwidth and diskspace?    Come on.....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Excuse me? Care to explain why this is <B>"pushing it"</B>?||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||05-22-2001||08:18 AM||||Man, I disapear for a day and the place goes crazy!  <P>You guys need to chill!  Every last STINKING one of you! <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||05-22-2001||08:44 AM||||Um... except for Cliff. He can un-chill as much as he likes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>However, I don't know if Grinthock will be able to chill for a while, as I imagine he's not much more than a smoking crater right now... ||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||05-22-2001||08:57 AM||||I can relate to where your coming from Cliff. I know the work that goes into a forum like this because the web is my business. I was pleasantly suprised when I stumbled across this place and appreciate the money and time you put into giving us a home. It would be a shame for it to be torn apart by pettiness.<P>Flame wars, well personally I try to avoid them as I know my feelings on any subject are probably different to 3 million other peoples opinions on the same. Wouldn't it be a boring world if they weren't. <P>People just have to learn to accept this and learn from other perspectives. Not go ape over an opinion you do not agree with. <P>If some one flames you, reply politely and explain the situation. If they continually flame you and scoff at your explanation you can do one thing that is beautiful about forums. Ignore them and don't reply.<P>We don't need petty arguments (isn't there enough crap in the real world already) and by the way, keep up the GREAT work Cliff. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero.gif"> <BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||14
Z||000010||84Bill||05-22-2001||08:59 AM||||Your right Cliff I'm sorry and thank you so much for removing them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000011||grinthock||05-22-2001||09:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B> Excuse me? Care to explain why this is [b]"pushing it"</B>?[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ignore that... I've had enough of this situation..... Sorry dude.....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||JSocha||05-22-2001||09:29 AM||||Thanks Cliff for the work you do maintaining this site and the dedication you yourself certainly have for the Fiero to have a site like this for all of us to become "FRIENDS" on and share information with our common interest, the FIERO. <P>It would be a shame just because a few bad apples, either it be people or it be comments, would force you to close this site down let alone force what apparently has now become two members to leave.  This is sad in itself.<P>This has become an informational source for myself and the comments or so called "Flame Wars" that have started should have been done via Email versus airing ones "laundry" out in public on this forum.<P>I sincerely hope that those with differing opinions, as much as it may hurt or burn you at the moment or how much you hate a comment from another member, will be mature enough to take the back "rumble" seat and not make enemys here and hurt the feelings of others by "directly" attacking and insulting them.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||p4n1c||05-22-2001||09:40 AM||||This is what happens with a public forum with over 2000 members.  Everyone should know the risk of posting something, words can be taken in a different context by anyone.  <P>Live and learn, I don't want to see someone leave over such petty comments.  If you are proud of your car, then you shouldn't care what people say.  Grin and bare it.  Hell, I drive a frickin' geriatric mobile.  But I'm proud of Ol' Rusty and I don't care what people say.<P>And as for insulting Lisa on posing on her car, she's 19(20?), all girls her age try to get attention by dressing up and flaunting.  It's what attracts guys to them.  I don't hold that against her, all the power to her, it seems to get all of you to trip over yourselves posting on her threads doesn't it?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As Cliff said, shake hands and let it go.  He pays for this forum out of his pocket and doesn't ask for anything in return.  He could just pull the plug.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000014||mrfixit58||05-22-2001||10:28 AM||||Life on the Forum was a lot easier before we hit 1000 members. People... please... before posting, take a deep breath, maybe get a drink of soda and be SURE when you submit or comment to a post your NOT over reacting. If you think someone else made an offending statement. Ask them to clarify it before you "start blasting away". <P>I read through the posts this morning and was just amazed to see (one person in particular) apologize for his choice of words used in his previous post and then his next statement was just as bad. And it would start all over again. Maybe it was too much caffeine. <P>If your get into an argument at work or at home, things are frequently said that you later regret. The heat of the moment kinda thing. The great thing about any message board is you can walk away for a few minutes and get your composure BEFORE you type a response. If you have to say something stupid, yell at the box that your staring at but keep your hands in your pocket until you blood pressure drops. Seems simple enough.<P>People GET A GRIP!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Raydar||05-22-2001||10:42 AM||||Glad I missed all of that. <P>This seems to illustrate the one biggest problem with text messaging in general. <BR>You can't see the persons face or hear the inflections in their voice. <BR>It's just words. We take words at face value and often miss the underlying, usually harmless, feelings. Being humans, we automatically assume the worst. <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroJoe||05-22-2001||10:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>This seems to illustrate the one biggest problem with text messaging in general. <BR>You can't see the persons face or hear the inflections in their voice. <BR>It's just words. We take words at face value and often miss the underlying, usually harmless, feelings. Being humans, we automatically assume the worst. <BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is so very very true.  I find myself in a pinch many times with instant messaging becuase people do not realize how sarcastic I can be and they can't tell that I am "typing this with a smile on my face".  That is why I always try to use smilely faces whenever possible and when it is needed.  <P>Edit: spelling and grammar<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cheever2||05-22-2001||10:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>You can't see the persons face or hear the inflections in their voice. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>That would not have mattered in this case.  Somebody chose to make a viscious personal attack.  I expect they'll get banned if they do it again.<P>And, Cliff:  who is "Louise"?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||LZeitgeist||05-22-2001||10:53 AM||||I think he was referring to the (supposed) inflection in Lisa's original post that starting the whole conflagration... but it's O.K. - it's over now... ||||reg||1
Z||000019||elfiero||05-22-2001||11:11 AM||||ya know I'll prolly catch some crap for this<BR>but,some of these people are pretty thin-<BR>skinned.What's the matter with a good'ol<BR>flamewar once in a while?If you don't want to<BR>play,don't respond!the real world isn't a<BR>warm&fuzzy place,why should it be any differ-<BR>ent in cyberspace?this forum is a crossection<BR>of the world so everyone has a different idea<BR>of what is and isn't nasty.Let's compare a<BR>person from the bronx and someone from malibu<BR>CA,see what I mean?If ya don't like what your<BR>reading,turn it OFF!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>PS-cliff,I'll understand if you won't put<BR>this on.||||reg||6
