Z||000021||LZeitgeist||05-22-2001||11:23 AM||||elfiero - <P>Do you like getting into screaming fights with your significant other? Do you like getting into fistfights when you're downtown or at the mall?<P>That's what a flamewar is akin to... but it rolls out of control online, though, because I've seen things said online that *nobody* would have the balls to say face-to-face... I've had things said to me online (not here - elsewhere) that I'd rip somebody's head off on the spot if they looked me in the eye and said it. <P>Flamewars aren't 'fun', and they don't belong here. Disagreements have their place here, just like everywhere else - nobody is going to agree all the time, whether it's a forum of 2 or 2,000. Everyone agreeing all the time is boring, and nothing gets learned or taught that way. But, this is a place for shared cameraderie and support, not for shredding other peoples' opinions/experiences.<P>Just my two cents' worth...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||JSocha||05-22-2001||11:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by elfiero:<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is a definate difference between a "Flame War" and an outright direct attack with the sole purpose of insulting someone's person.  <P>I'm sure you as well as others all still have "personal feelings" and "boundries", regardless if it is in person and/or in cyber-space, to what you would feel as appropriate versus inappropriate comments that you would wish others to respect and consider.<P>A fellow member here on the forum didn't need to get blasted the way she did for what I see and feel was an "innocent" comment blown way out of proportion.<P>No one here or anyplace else I feel deserves that treatment.  Lisa; you; myself; or any other.<P>If nothing else, "Do onto others as you want done onto yourself".<P>A few time's I have personally went offline with an email so it wouldn't end up going way overboard, get blown out of proportion or so I got clarification both ways from either a statement I made or a statement someone else made that may be related to me.<P>That I feel is the appropriate way to handle it.  I don't know if FieroLisa or Cameron are reading this and are willing to confirm this.<P>BTW, does anyone know what happened to Cameron.  He hasn't posted anything lately.  Going to have to email him and see what's up.<P>Cameron, you will get mail later today!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Oreif||05-22-2001||11:35 AM||||Well just to state my opinion, I read thru the posts in the other threads. I think 84Bill got a little defensive, But he did attempt to make amends, ease the tension, and apologized to Lisa. Now the real instigator in the threads went way too far. The other member even went so far as to continue the "flames" in other threads not related to the initial thread. This I feel is wrong. From the few other threads where he attacks Lisa, I think he just got some twisted idea he was the leader of some crusade to berate Lisa. It is he who should apologize to Lisa and the rest of us.<BR>It's one thing to have a "flame war" in a specific thread, But it's another to go to other threads/topic's and flame the person there too.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000024||grinthock||05-22-2001||11:39 AM||||Again allow me to say;<P>It's over, it's finished... I do apoligize as I have 2 or 3 times, but it's warranted again....  Allow me to list the names of those offended and affected by this apology order.<P>Lisa (The Official Miss Fiero 2001 - Yes it is true!) {Ok JM fuelled my passion a bit can you understand ?}<P>Cliff Pennock (Ok I apoligize for starting a flame war on your box dude, sorry!)<P>84Bill (Sorry dude I got you flamed!)<P>And anyone else who was offended....  Let's all get along.  Note to self -- Don't write on pennocks after a few Brava's it's NOT a good idea.||||reg||1
Z||000025||stimpy||05-22-2001||11:45 AM||||I've been known to relish some banter now and then, but I've also been involved in cases where it's gone way over the edge. I've told myself "Screw this place, I'm Audi" due to what others have posted. I've also crossed the line, making a total ass of myself. Tempers do flare occaisionally, but sometimes you gotta recognize when it's turned personal.  <P>I think 84Bill seems apologetic about bringing this mess up, and it does take a grown-up to admit their faux pas without making excuses. I hope Lisa can forget about all the hoo-hah and get back to enjoying the forum with the rest of us.<P>As far as grinthock, you got a lot to learn before you are one of the "big boyz".  Quit making excuses for the mess you made, and make amends. That's how "big boyz" act. <BR>(edited because as I typed this, grinthock was making some attempt to do right. Still making excuses though. Be real, dude.)<p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||FieroLisa||05-22-2001||11:50 AM||||grinthock: I don't know why I'm wasting my time replying to you, but why do you think using my ex-boyfriend is going to help your case?  Suuure we broke up- it happens. And not only that but its none of your business. The only thing you or he can accuse me of is working my ass off to make the relationship work. Driving 8 hours each way to Canada at least once a month. Sure, did that. Paid over $100 in phone bills every month: Ah, yep add that to the list too. I was an excellent girlfriend, and he knows it, even if he might be saying otherwise to you or whoever. I know he has a new girlfriend, that's fine. Moving on happens- including to me. I'm not sitting in my bed weeping about my ex. Which is why I think its funny that youre bringing this up. I have moved on, he has moved on. It's your turn.<P>Don't you understand your digging yourself into a deeper hole here? If anyone on this forum respects you and what you have said here, I wonder who they are. <P>If you spend your time concerning yourself with my old relationships, please, for your own sake, go out and find your own girlfriend!<P>Oh and ya know, I honestly don't care what you think about my sig pic. Last time I heard you had one of my pics as your desktop on the computer.<P>If you want to continue arguing with me, just email me, don't leave it here.<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48495967&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
