Z||000047||Jaygee79||05-22-2001||02:06 PM||||Am I the only one that saw absolutely nothing wrong is Lisa's original post?  I didn't take it to mean that she doesn't appreciate the trophy.  I don't know, maybe it's some secret female language or something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Grinthock, heed your own advice and LET IT GO.  You continue to post saying that you are done with it.  If you're done with it then STOP POSTING ABOUT IT.<P>Lisa, I admire you for what you have done to your car.  I saw it at the show and it was amazing!  I wish I knew enough to be able to work on my car like that.  You should be proud of yourself, and you deserved that trophy no matter what anyone says.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000048||AkursedX||05-22-2001||02:28 PM||||I knew I shouldn't of went to sleep!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  To be honest, I was laughing my a** off throughout that entire flamewar.  IT'S THE INTERNET!!!  Who really gives a crap what a person who has never met you thinks of you?  Alot of people have taken alot of things way too personally, and then of course there was just flat out stupidity.  It never ceases to amaze me how people's ego's can get so easily offended.    <BR>But to be honest, this was funny to me last night, now it's just pitiful.  There is no need to be carrying on about a topic like this.  <BR>I'm sure I'm not the only one who has noticed alot of "bickering" on this forum as of late, and I find it quite annoying when I got to sift through numerous topics about the same flame so I can find a topic that is something that I might gain some sort of knowledge out of!  So, if you people must flame, could you please at least keep it to one topic??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So anyways, everyone kiss and make up, and lets get back to being the best forum on the net!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000049||p4n1c||05-22-2001||02:35 PM||||Right now the phrase, "forgive and forget" comes to mind, especially when dealing with something so impersonal as the Internet.<P>Misinterpretation of people's words on here is so easy because there are no feelings behind the words and there is no real way to tell of the sincerity.  <P>I know it's hard because of the personal attacks, but let's focus the energy on something more productive.  You know, this is how wars are started and people die.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000050||Voytek||05-22-2001||03:07 PM||||Ok.  I couldn't resist this any longer<BR>First we must start by prying some of you off Cliff's butt.  While we all appreciate what he's doing, I think he himself enjoys reading some controversial opinions.  If he posts a banner asking for money, I think most of us will be there.<P>As far as the other two threads go, they're very interesting.  To all of you who say there shoudn't be any flaming here and only good wholesome Fiero talk: if people don't want to get burned or do not enjoy reading flame wars, they always have the choice of going to another topic.  If we were always having group hugs and kisses, things would be just too boring.<BR>STIMPY: you NEVER seize to pi*s me off.  Why do you have to drag that 'you Canadians / us Americans' thing into every disagreement???!!  Grinthok is another member on the Forum.  If I don't like YOUR opinion, I won't call you a '(insert word)' American, I'll just call you a dumb sh*t!<BR>Oh, and I think anyone who can't accept about 100 apologies shouldn't be on this Forum 'cause they're bound to get burned at one time or another and can't expect an apology every time (I'm not refering to FieroLisa who hasn't said much about the apologies, I'm talking about all others who continue to dismiss all apologies like THEY're the ones who got insulted) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
